  "verbalization": "Arundinol B is implicated in the biological activity of SNU-387, which is a target of multiple compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol. All these compounds share a common target of LAPC4, suggesting a potential pathway where Arundinol B may influence LAPC4 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence indicates that Arundinol B acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn targets LAPC4, establishing a chain of molecular relationships. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust connection, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The presence of multiple compounds with similar targets implies that Arundinol B may exert its effects through a broader biological mechanism, possibly involving the modulation of signaling pathways or cellular processes that are also affected by LAPC4.",
